  vk26-alice-2-the-hash-tested-first-1.txt: J1 NO [README.md:328, README.md:329, README.md:330, board/round1.txt:1, README.md:301] The board log in the bundle holds only the page summary line and a few BITS lines. The claimed TRNG figures (longest runs 11, 12 and 11; 516/508, 501/522, 518/527 equal to the window's first) and the per-round, per-code table (README.md:312-316) cannot be checked against it. The LED observation (README.md:301) names no UF2 name or SHA-256, so it cannot stand as a recorded observation.
  vk26-alice-2-the-hash-tested-first-2.txt: J1 NO [README.md:328, README.md:329, README.md:330, board/round1.txt:1] README.md:328-330 gives the TRNG draws' statistics (longest runs 11, 12 and 11; 516 and 508, 501 and 522, 518 and 527 of each window equal to its first). Nothing in the bundle supports these numbers, and the log in the bundle has no BITS lines for rounds 7–9, where the TRNG draws are. The other board claims match board/round1.txt:1 (18 streams, 4 refused, 3 start-up, 7 outputs) and the passing round1.txt checks in capture.txt, and the proof and mutant claims match the theorems and capture.
  vk26-alice-2-the-hash-tested-first-3.txt: J1 NO [README.md:328, README.md:329, README.md:330, README.md:300, README.md:301] The TRNG draw figures ("longest runs 11, 12 and 11; 516 and 508, 501 and 522, 518 and 527") come from the board log. The log in the bundle holds only a few lines (BITS lines of the spoiled stream, round 6 stream 1, plus one status line), none of them the TRNG draws in rounds 7–9, and no gate output reproduces these numbers. The LED observation (README.md:301, also README.md:24–25) does not say which UF2 was flashed, so it is not a recorded observation of the required kind. The remaining claims (theorems, 112 instructions, counts, the 11 mutants, the 18-of-18 summary) match the Lean files and capture.txt.
  vk26-alice-2-the-hash-tested-first-2.txt: J2 NO [README.md:18, README.md:19, ../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:102, ../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:103, ../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:107, ../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:108, ../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:109, ../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:443] `from_boot` (../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:438-443) is of `from_boot` form, and its codes, counts and KAT-failure case match the text. But the README's headline says that with code 0 the output at 0x2400 is written "and no other byte changed" (README.md:19). The proved memory, `after` → `writeBytes (katted …) OUT …` (../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:109), also has `HASH`'s KAT answer written at 0x360 (../lean/Alice/Trust.lean:103), so the theorem contradicts that claim rather than supporting it.
